==English==
[[Image:Walnut03.jpg|thumb|right|The expression refers to the tidy, compact package.]]

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|la|in nuce}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-au-in a nutshell.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{head|en|adverb}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} In summary; [[briefly]] or [[simply]].
#: {{ux|en|He had a lot to say, but his answer, '''in a nutshell''', was no.}}
#* '''2019''', Daniel Taylor, ''Lionel Messi magic puts Barcelona in command of semi-final with Liverpool'' (in ''The Guardian'', 1 May 2019)[https://www.theguardian.com/football/2019/may/01/barcelona-liverpool-champions-league-match-report]
#*: Sadio Mané wasted a glorious chance in the first half and, late on, Mohamed Salah turned his shot against a post after a goal-line clearance had spun his way. That, '''in a nutshell''', perhaps sums up the difference between Messi and the players on the next rung below – the ones who can be described as great footballers without necessarily being football greats.
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|I|The yarns of seamen have a direct simplicity, the whole meaning of which lies '''within the shell of a cracked nut'''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|at the end of the day}}, {{l|en|in short}}; see also [[Thesaurus:in summary]]

